From 833fe707294873291063a0abca54a7335e2d3c41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] init: no RUST_BACKTRACE=1 for the services and the login
 session

init started every service with RUST_BACKTRACE=1. getty passes its
environment on to login and the shell, so every program a user started had it
too. A tool that returns an error from main, such as ping with a name
that does not resolve, then printed "Stack backtrace:" with frames that
are all <unknown>: the binaries have no symbols. It tells nothing and
looks like a crash.

Start the services without it. A panic still prints its message and
source location. Whoever wants a backtrace sets RUST_BACKTRACE in the
shell or in a unit's envs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 init/src/main.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/src/main.rs b/init/src/main.rs
index c2aff750..ac961b94 100644
--- a/init/src/main.rs
+++ b/init/src/main.rs
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ impl InitConfig {
         Self {
             log_debug,
             skip_cmd,
-            envs: BTreeMap::from([("RUST_BACKTRACE".to_owned(), "1".into())]),
+            envs: BTreeMap::new(),
             cwd: "/scheme/initfs".into(),
         }
     }
